  "worked_solution": "The intermediate value theorem can be applied to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nThe function is discontinuous at the values of $x$ which makes the denominator equal to zero.\n\nSetting the denominator equal to zero, we have ${x}^{2}+5x+6=0,$ which corresponds to $x=-3$ or $x=-2.$ \n\nWe conclude that the intermediate value theorem can be applied to the function $f(x)$ only on closed intervals that do not contain the points $x=-3$ or $x=-2.$ \n\nFrom the given options, only the interval $[-1,3]$ is allowed. The intervals $[-8,-3)$ and $(-2,1]$ are not closed, while $[-5,-3]$ and $[-4,-2]$ contain the point $x=-3.$",
